.TH HORSEPOWERD 8 "November 2026" "HorsePower 1.0.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
horsepowerd \- HorsePower power metering service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B horsepowerd
.RB [ \-\-foreground ]
.RB [ \-\-db
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-interval
.IR SECONDS ]
.RB [ \-\-retention\-days
.IR DAYS ]
.RB [ \-\-bus
.RB { system | session }]
.RB [ \-\-verbose ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B horsepowerd
samples the hardware energy counter once per second, keeps a running total and
writes it to a local SQLite database. It is a compiled Rust binary and links
only the C library; SQLite is built in. It owns the D-Bus name
.B org.horsepower.Daemon
and serves two methods:
.TP
.B org.horsepower.Daemon.GetStatus
Returns a dictionary with the live wattage, today's energy, the lifetime
energy, the sensor description and any error message. The
.B components
entry is an array of
.RI ( key ", " label ", " watts )
triples giving the per-part breakdown. A part that this machine cannot measure
is absent from the array rather than present with a zero value.
.TP
.B org.horsepower.Daemon.GetHistory
Takes a number of minutes and returns a list of
.RI ( timestamp ", " watts ", " watt_hours )
triples, one per minute.
.PP
A
.B StatusChanged
signal is emitted after every sample and
.B HistoryChanged
after each flush to disk.
.PP
The service is started on demand through D-Bus and is enabled at boot by
.BR horsepower.service .
Running as root is required on kernels that restrict energy counters to the
owner of the file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-foreground
Stay in the foreground. This is the normal mode under systemd.
.TP
.BI \-\-db " PATH"
Database file. Defaults to
.IR /var/lib/horsepower/power.db .
.TP
.BI \-\-interval " SECONDS"
Sampling interval, minimum 0.2. Defaults to 1.
.TP
.BI \-\-retention\-days " DAYS"
How long per-minute samples are kept. Daily totals are never deleted.
Defaults to 90.
.TP
.BI \-\-bus " system|session"
Which bus to use. Defaults to
.IR system .
.TP
.B \-\-sysfs\-root
Alternative sysfs class root, used by the test suite. Pointing it at a
directory tree containing
.I powercap/
and
.I power_supply/
lets the service be exercised without hardware.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Log at debug level.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/horsepower/power.db
SQLite database. Owner root, mode 0600.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR horsepower (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
